    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Since the probability of rain on each day is independent, the probability of both days raining together is the product of the probabilities of each individual day raining. In this case, the probability of rain on Saturday is $60\\%$, which can be written as $0.60$, and the probability of rain on Sunday is $25\\%$, which can be written as $0.25$. The probability that it will rain on both days is therefore $(0.60)(0.25)=0.15=15\\%$.\nThe answer is: 15",
